   "source": [
    "# Step 5: Compute text Statistics for Vectorization"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8b8ea9a8-0f49-40e0-88a5-93a2279829bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1) Computes the average number of words per SMS, used as sequence length for padding.\n",
    "   \n",
    "2) Estimates vocabulary size by counting unique tokens across all messages.\n",
    "\n",
    "3) Prints basic dataset statistics for reference."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "1ac5f5df-fc9e-476f-9db3-a8528808bb7d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Data Loaded. Training samples: 4457\n",
      "Average words per message: 16\n",
      "Approximate vocabulary size: 15686\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "avg_words_len = round(sum([len(i.split())\n",
    "                      for i in df['Text']]) / len(df['Text']))\n",
    "total_words_length = len(set(\" \".join(df['Text']).split()))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Data Loaded. Training samples: {len(X_train_np)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Average words per message: {avg_words_len}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Approximate vocabulary size: {total_words_length}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "67c43fbd-4a80-41b9-8082-3f0c97743b0b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Step 6: Helper functions for training and evaluation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5e8466c6-3243-4596-9ef2-936c428dd651",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- compile_and_fit centralizes the compile + train logic for all models.\n",
    "  \n",
    "- Uses binary_crossentropy and accuracy for binary classification.\n",
    "  \n",
    "- Trains on training data and validates on the test data, returning training history.\n",
    "\n",
    "- get_metrics predicts labels, rounds probabilities to 0 or 1 and computes accuracy, precision, recall and F1-score."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "6f573ac8-5aab-4641-a1f9-ee2d07970b2f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def compile_and_fit(model, epochs=5):\n",
    "    model.compile(\n",
    "        optimizer='adam',\n",
    "        loss='binary_crossentropy',\n",
    "        metrics=['accuracy']\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    history = model.fit(\n",
    "        X_train_np,\n",
    "        y_train_np,\n",
    "        epochs=epochs,\n",
    "        validation_data=(X_test_np, y_test_np)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    return history\n",
    "\n",
    "def get_metrics(model, X, y):\n",
    "    y_preds = np.round(model.predict(X))\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        'accuracy': accuracy_score(y, y_preds),\n",
    "        'precision': precision_score(y, y_preds),\n",
    "        'recall': recall_score(y, y_preds),\n",
    "        'f1-score': f1_score(y, y_preds)\n",
    "    }"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7214002c-3fe7-4446-ad2e-8bc10061c6c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Step 7: Create the TextVectorization layer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d393f020-6c80-4011-b240-fa5fe20d643d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Creates a TextVectorization layer to convert raw text into integer sequences.\n",
    "- Limits the vocabulary size to total_words_length unique words.\n",
    "- Standardizes text by lowercasing and stripping punctuation.\n",
    "- Pads or truncates each sequence to avg_words_len tokens.\n",
    "- Adapts the layer on training data to learn the vocabulary distribution."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "fdbd8e42-36d2-45a4-9f33-c4703525a89f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from tensorflow.keras.layers import TextVectorization\n",
    "text_vec = TextVectorization(\n",
    "    max_tokens=total_words_length,\n",
    "    standardize='lower_and_strip_punctuation',\n",
    "    output_mode='int',\n",
    "    output_sequence_length=avg_words_len\n",
    ")\n",
    "text_vec.adapt(X_train_np)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "655c77e4-af72-4b27-8084-5f331ca97123",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Step 8: Model 1 – Dense embedding model (build and train)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "95f9d1c1-3977-4689-9e91-cce120f3250d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Defines an input layer that expects string tensors.\n",
    "- Applies the TextVectorization layer to convert text into token IDs.\n",
    "- Uses an Embedding layer to learn dense vector representations for each word.\n",
    "- Applies GlobalAveragePooling1D to compress each sequence into a single vector.\n",
    "- Adds a dense hidden layer with ReLU activation for non-linearity.\n",
    "- Outputs a single sigmoid unit for binary spam/ham prediction.\n",
    "- Compiles and trains the model using the shared compile_and_fit function."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "fa6f1c22-ae0d-425a-8a3d-9c05f60333b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
